## 3. Content Blocks — Text

### Editor Toolbar
- Displays the current page title as a bold label (shows "Select a page" when no page is loaded).
- Block creation buttons: **+ Text**, **+ Table**, **+ List**, **Template**.
- Formatting buttons: **B**, **I**, **H1**, **H2**, **<>**, **🔗**, **•**.
- **Font size combo box** ("Size:") with sizes 9–32, applied to the focused element.
- A vertical "|" separator divides block creation buttons from formatting buttons.

### Add a text block
- Click **"+ Text"** in the editor toolbar.
- **Block placement:** Click on the canvas first, then click "+ Text" — the block appears at the click position. Without a prior click, the block is placed below all existing blocks. If all blocks have default position (0,0), they are auto-arranged in a grid (5 columns, 280px horizontal / 200px vertical spacing).

### Edit content
- Click the preview area to switch to edit mode (cursor moves to end).
- Click outside or press Tab to return to preview.
- Markdown is rendered as HTML in preview (fenced code, tables, line breaks via `nl2br` supported).
- Content starting with `<` is treated as raw HTML.
- Preview updates in real-time as you type.

### Formatting toolbar
| Button | Shortcut | Action |
|--------|----------|--------|
| **B** | `Ctrl+B` | Toggles bold on selected text or for new input |
| **I** | `Ctrl+I` | Toggles italic on selected text or for new input |
| **H1** | — | Toggles heading 1 (large bold) on selected text or for new input |
| **H2** | — | Toggles heading 2 (medium bold) on selected text or for new input |
| **<>** | — | Toggles code formatting (monospace with background) on selected text or for new input |
| **🔗** | — | Opens file dialog to attach a file or insert a link |
| **•** | — | Toggles bullet list on current paragraph or selected paragraphs |
| **Size:** | — | Font size combo box: applies to focused element (header, text, table cell, or list item). Sizes: 9–32. |

- Formatting buttons show checked state when the style is active at cursor position
- Buttons update their state when focus changes between text areas
- Clicking an active button toggles the style off
- Formatting works in text blocks, table cells, and task text areas
- Toolbar buttons maintain focus on the active text edit, allowing formatting to be applied without losing cursor position
- Button state updates only on focus changes to prevent crashes during typing
- Bullet list toggle validates block state before accessing text list to prevent crashes
- Multiple bullet lists can be created in the same text box or table cell; toggling off exits the current list and creates a new paragraph
- When switching from preview to edit mode, formatting is applied with a delay to ensure the editor is fully ready

### Embedded Task Lists in Text Blocks
- Click **"+ List"** while a text block has focus → an embedded task list is added inside the text block.
- Each embedded list has: drag handle ("⠿"), "Tasks" label, "+ Add Task" button, and "×" remove button.
- Tasks within embedded lists support: checkbox toggle, multi-line text, recurrence, and per-task delete.
- Embedded lists are serialized as JSON within the text block's content and persist across sessions.
- The "+ Add Task" button in the block header adds a task to the currently active embedded list.

### Block Header
- Each block has an **editable header** (click to edit; defaults to block type name, e.g., "text").
- **Enter** in the header accepts the edit (clears focus). **Tab** moves focus out.
- Placeholder text shows the block type when header is empty.
- **Horizontal alignment:** ⫷ (left), ⫿ (center), ⫸ (right) buttons.
- **Vertical alignment:** ↥ (top), ↕ (middle), ↧ (bottom) buttons (only enabled when header is focused).
- **Header font size:** Use the toolbar "Size:" combo while the header has focus.
- **Header height resize:** Drag the handle between the header and the block body to change header height.
- All header properties (text, alignment, font size, height) are persisted in the database.

### Delete a block
- Click the **"×"** button in the block header (no confirmation, undoable).
- **Keyboard:** `Delete` key deletes all selected blocks on the canvas.
- **Keyboard:** `Ctrl+D` deletes all selected blocks (when focus is NOT in a text edit).

### Multi-select blocks on canvas
- **Ctrl+click** or **Shift+click** to select multiple blocks on the canvas.
- Selected blocks display a 2px indigo border with light background.
- Clicking a block without modifiers selects only that block.
- Clicking empty canvas space clears the selection.

### Resize a block
- **Bottom resize handle** — drag up/down to change height, drag left/right to change width.
- **Bottom-right corner** (24px dotted area) — 2D resize: drag to change both width and height simultaneously.
- **Right edge** — hover near the right edge of any block (cursor changes to ↔), then click and drag to change width.

### Canvas behavior
- The canvas is **vertically infinite** — scrolling near the bottom extends it automatically (no horizontal scrollbar).
- **Right edge is a hard boundary** — blocks cannot be dragged or resized past the right edge of the canvas.
- Position (`pos_x`, `pos_y`) is persisted in the database.

### Move blocks (free-form canvas)
- Blocks are positioned on a **free-form canvas** (no layout constraints).
- Drag the **"⋮⋮"** handle **or the header area** to freely reposition a block.
- Blocks can overlap and be placed anywhere within the canvas bounds.
- **Clicking** a block brings it to the front (z-order).
- Drag is constrained to canvas bounds (blocks cannot be dragged off left/right edges).
- Position is saved immediately after drag release.

### Auto-fit to content
- Blocks automatically resize their height to fit content when not manually resized.
- Once a block is manually resized (via any handle), auto-fit is disabled for that block.
- New blocks default to 200px height and 1/3 of the canvas width.

### Scroll behavior
- After adding a new block, the canvas scrolls to make it visible.

